SUMMARY:I Cheerfully Refuse by Leif Enger
DESCRIPTION:Post-Apocalyptic Book Club - Toronto Chapter\nThis time we'll 
 be reading *I Cheerfully Refuse* by Leif Enger. Here's the blurb:\n\nSet i
 n a not-too-distant America\, *I Cheerfully Refuse* is the tale of Rainy\,
  an aspiring musician setting sail on Lake Superior in search of his depar
 ted\, deeply beloved\, bookselling wife. An endearing bear of an Orphean n
 arrator\, he seeks refuge in the harbors\, fogs\, and remote islands of th
 e inland sea. After encountering lunatic storms and rising corpses from th
 e warming depths\, he eventually lands to find an increasingly desperate a
 nd illiterate people\, a malignant billionaire ruling class\, a crumbled i
 nfrastructure\, and a lawless society. As his guileless nature begins to m
 ake an inadvertent rebel of him\, Rainy’s private quest for the love of 
 his life grows into something wider and wilder\, sweeping up friends and f
 oes alike in his wake.\n\nThe book is available here:\n\nAmazon- Hardcover
 \, Paperback\, eBook\, Audiobook:\nhttps://a.co/d/05tztwov\n\nIndigo- Pape
 rback:\nhttps://www.indigo.ca/products/i-cheerfully-refuse-1?variant=46334
 710218962\n\nKobo- eBook:\nhttps://www.kobo.com/ca/en/ebook/i-cheerfully-r
 efuse-1?sId=4a8880c0-6bbe-44cc-922f-30d4fa9f3559&ssId=KIjaRjuRu_SCDHu7jYsl
 f&cPos=2\n\nToronto Public Library:\nhttps://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/reco
 rd/S234C4485546\n\nLooking forward to seeing you there!
